Subject: [PATCH 08/14] setup, serve: the installer and Settings expose the
 on-disk layer (off by default)

setup.py asks for it (--conversation-cache-spill-dir, --system-prompt-cache) and
creates a feature's folder only when it is turned on; runconfig.py makes the same
keys editable in the Settings view (a bare flag, a folder, an enum and the
limits); server.py reads the two features' log lines so the Monitor card shows
what the disk holds.  With nothing set, no flag is added and nothing is written.
The launcher keeps its own defaults: the layer's folders are the repo's slots/,
and this install points them at its data disk by flag.
